  "log/2026-08-28T21-17-54.580-07-00-retrospective-with-enforcement.md": "# Retrospective with Enforcement — 2026-08-28\n\nEvidence window: 2026-08-22T04:17:54.580Z through 2026-08-29T04:17:54.580Z.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- GitHub reports 30 closed issues and 56 merged pull requests in the window.\n- Shipped highlights: governance and architecture (#7/#22/#14/#4/#9 via PRs #12/#24/#17/#25/#26/#45); Phase 1A implementation and hardening (#39/#55/#72/#75/#64/#63/#71/#85/#87 via PRs #46/#78/#80/#81/#82/#83/#84/#86/#89); quality/operations and documentation (#61/#97/#94/#96/#116 via PRs #77/#98/#105/#103/#117); state allowlist repair in PR #120.\n- Current queue: 27 open issues: 22 labeled `status:backlog`, two `status:branch-only` (#8, #42), and three `status:merged` (#3, #6, #10). The only open PR is #50.\n- Phase 1A exit remains open in #44/#62: remaining gates include trusted release signing, encrypted database plus Data Protection clean-host restored sign-in, approved update/rollback evidence, and human SLO/RPO/RTO/cost/residual-risk decisions.\n- #66 still requires an explicit final ADR packet/residual-risk decision. #73 and #74 still require human governance/provider-scope decisions.\n- #102 terminated its selective-CI feasibility window without spend because no qualifying natural prose-only candidate existed; the shadow workflow is disabled and promotion remains evidence-blocked.\n- #104 has native containment (`allow_auto_merge=false`) and reviewed repository scaffolding, but operational acceptance remains blocked on a separately authorized/provisioned non-Actions App worker and live canaries.\n- No prior retrospective log existed in the runtime-owned `log` directory during this seven-day window. The configured `retro-enforcement` skill was unavailable.\n\n## Root causes\n\nEvidence:\n- Several implementation artifacts merged while acceptance, human decision, or external evidence gates intentionally remained open (#3, #6, #10, #44, #62, #66, #73, #74).\n- Open issue